# Hubble CLI Troubleshooting & eBPF Flow Inspection Guide

This guide covers real-time network flow analysis, policy verification, and packet drop inspection using the Cilium
`hubble` CLI on the control plane node.

---

## 1. Prerequisites & Status Verification

Ensure Cilium Hubble relay and port-forwarding are active on `kube-control-plane`:

```bash
# Verify Cilium cluster health and Hubble status
cilium status --wait

# Start Hubble port-forward in background if not already running
cilium hubble port-forward &

# Verify local Hubble connectivity
hubble status
```

---

## 2. Tracing NetworkPolicy Drops in Real Time

When troubleshooting NetworkPolicies, use `--verdict DROPPED` to capture packets rejected by Linux kernel eBPF map
rules:

```bash
# Watch dropped packets live across the default namespace
hubble observe --namespace {{ cks_lab_netpol_namespace | default('default') }} --verdict DROPPED -f

# Filter drops specifically originating from the test client pod
hubble observe --pod {{ cks_lab_netpol_namespace | default('default') }}/netpol-test-client --verdict DROPPED

# Filter drops targeting the internal-api backend pod
hubble observe --pod {{ cks_lab_netpol_namespace | default('default') }}/internal-api --verdict DROPPED
```

### Common Drop Reasons in Hubble Output

- `Policy denied (INGRESS)`: Inbound traffic rejected by a default-deny policy or missing ingress whitelist rule.
- `Policy denied (EGRESS)`: Outbound request rejected by missing CoreDNS (UDP 53) or missing egress whitelist rules.

---

## 3. Monitoring DNS Queries and Resolutions

To debug DNS issues when pods cannot resolve in-cluster or external hostnames:

```bash
# Observe DNS resolution flows live in the scenario namespace
hubble observe --namespace {{ cks_lab_netpol_namespace | default('default') }} --protocol dns -f

# Monitor CoreDNS traffic specifically in kube-system
hubble observe --namespace kube-system --protocol dns -f
```

---

## 4. Inspecting Microservice Traffic Flows

```bash
# Trace HTTP requests and response codes across namespaces
hubble observe --namespace {{ cks_lab_netpol_namespace | default('default') }} --protocol http -f

# Compact one-line flow format for high-throughput troubleshooting
hubble observe --namespace {{ cks_lab_netpol_namespace | default('default') }} -o compact
```
